Home/End keys open the pager help instead of moving. hat routes Home/End through reencodeCursor -> libvterm encodeKey, which emits xterm-style \eOH / \e[H, but hat advertises TERM=tmux-256color whose terminfo declares khome=\e[1~ and kend=\e[4~ (mode-independent). less keys off terminfo, does not match \e[H, and processes the bare H as help. Arrows work (tmux kcuu1=\eOA matches libvterm app-mode). FIX: send fixed \e[1~ / \e[4~ for Home/End and drop them from reencodeCursor cursorKeyOf; keep the 4 arrows DECCKM-encoded. Verified via infocmp tmux-256color vs xterm-256color. | id:0352e506940a61414118392a36c6d132b021f9a1
