option show has no per-scope read-back: cmdShow always reads the global st.options cache, so a session/window/pane-scoped set + show -v/-A/-u/-p do not resolve (upstream options-scope.sh); cmdShow also prints scalars unquoted where tmux quotes string values (show-options-output.sh). | id:08240654e34bafdfddb94fd5050297cb8652644d
tmux passthrough: honor or loudly-log payloads hat does not answer. hat now answers OSC 10/11 and DEC 2031 queries wrapped in DCS tmux passthrough (bug 16 fix). Other payloads -- OSC 52 clipboard, OSC 12 cursor color, OSC 4 palette -- are still silently dropped per allow-passthrough-off. Decide per-sequence: forward to outer terminal, answer from hat state, or log so we stop silently discarding. | id:0b5ef18f6268b708cf75da2db7481cc10ea463c5
bracket pipe-pane teardown: reader thread + subprocess + stdin handle are released by hand-called killThread/hClose/terminateProcess (Server.hs ~3897-3931) instead of being a structural sub-resource of the pane. Mirror startPaneReader's scoped ownership. Severity B, from bug 9 audit. | id:0f8e4e961a0a1a4a5150f3c143767f98521088b4
