Zooming a pane running/just-exiting less writes persistent garbage (help + file interleaved, plus one line of stale colored cells). INVESTIGATION (2026-08-02): RULED OUT emulator+C layer -- grid clean after alt-exit (no resize), alt-exit+resize, resize-while-in-alt (3 repl probes + EmulatorSpec guard); hat_shim memsets so no uninitialized memory. RULED OUT client alt-exit repaint (passing IntegrationSpec test) and zoom-of-less happy path (clean). LIKELY ROOT CAUSE: reconcilePaneSizes resized the pty BEFORE the emulator, so the SIGWINCH one-shot redraw could hit the old-size emulator and persist as garbage. FIX LANDED bc78e09: Emu.resize before Pty.resize (model before signaling child) + regression tests 4dd3eb8. CAVEAT: could NOT reproduce deterministically -- the race needs the pane actively OUTPUTTING (readLoop holding the emulator lock) during resize, which static less-help does not. Correct ordering invariant regardless; VERIFY LIVE (zoom during active output). If it recurs, add a stress/seam bug-capture test. | id:a3820c67f631f59f0ebafc2ce4df8fd985834f0d
