if-shell config-load ordering race: config loads in a background thread so new can spawn a pane before the config default-terminal is set -- pane TERM races the config under load (upstream if-shell-TERM.sh, FLAKY). Real fix = command-queue ordering so client commands wait for config to drain WITHOUT deadlocking a nested $TMUX-in-if-shell. This is the deliberate next task after the upstream xfail triage. | id:cd516e22b26d91258f263e1033d9fbf4ae194ed8
