withLogger bracketed lifetime: the logger's file handle + drain thread (Hat.Log) are opened/forked without structural teardown. Wrap as withLogger (handle + drain under withAsync, flush/close on exit). Also unblocks flushing the log before a restart-server self-exec. Severity B, from bug 9 audit (docs/resource-cleanup-audit.md). | id:e070613dd524ef3376db3aeb34a9328d00254355
[FEAT] restart-client: in-place restart of currently-attached client. no-op if not presently attached | id:e510309d5357f9040f34997e80e4b9256d331817
