FLAKE restart-server reload: integration test 'restart-server reloads in place, keeping the pane's program alive' (IntegrationSpec ~1861) flakes -- reattach's list-panes -F #{pane_pid} returns empty (pidAfter=""), racing the reload's restore gate before pane adoption completes. PRE-EXISTING on origin/main (381c5f9), load-sensitive: ~1/3 in full parallel suite, up to 9/15 under concurrent-build load; passed 4/4 in clean sequential runs. Not a crash/orphan -- a sync gap. Fix direction: a happens-before so the query awaits restore completion (cf. the zoom-reconcile fix). Same area as the Jul 28 reload-crash work. | id:f3ac1db72520d3e5d4c6cbcb2f573782c6de26ab
restart-server reload drops the pane emulator's app-set modes, so a surviving app stops reacting to OS colorscheme changes: adoptPane builds a fresh emulator (colorReport=False) and ReloadPane carries no mode flags, so the app's DEC ?2031 subscription is lost across a reload. notifySubscribedPanes then skips it (a NEW pane re-subscribes and works). Fix: carry the ?2031 subscription (min) or all app-set modes (mouse/focus/bracketed-paste/DECCKM/colorReport) across the reload handover -- additive ReloadPane field, bump reloadEra, add a corpus vector; adoptPane seeds the emulator + re-pushes current scheme once. Family: bug 16 (2-3s gsettings lag) and bug 27 (reload live screen/scrollback). | id:f3b96451f30d2ddcedbb3b4fffe8a57a28549fb7
suspend (C-z) then fg of an inner app leaks a terminal query response (e.g. '9;4;0') as literal text into the app's input instead of being consumed as an escape sequence | id:f6797ecc02d40d3867ced6440b5e68cf2d528e0a
Recognize F1-F12, Insert, BackTab (Shift-Tab), and modified specials (Shift/Ctrl-arrows, S-Home etc.) as named keys so they can be bound, and normalize forwarded keys to tmux-256color terminfo rather than passing the outer terminal bytes verbatim. Today the tokenizer swallows unrecognized CSI/SS3 as "Unknown" and passes the raw bytes through: this WORKS when the outer terminal encodes a key the same as tmux-256color (true for \E[N~ and SS3 F1-4), but such keys cannot be bound by name, and a divergent outer terminal would mis-send them. Home/End were the only actively-broken case and are fixed (send-Home/End-as-terminfo commit). Lower priority: forwarding is correct for standard terminals; this is bindability + robustness. Audit: infocmp tmux-256color, 2026-08-02. | id:fad4fd9da74b450624c035a68ad3b81b72a78932
escape-time is a silent no-op: stored in Options but read by nothing. ESC disambiguation in Hat.Server.Keys.tokenizeKeys is hardcoded to escape-time-0 semantics (a lone trailing ESC = Escape). Fix needs input-path timing: buffer a trailing lone ESC, arm an escape-time-ms timer in the server event loop, coalesce with the next bytes if they arrive first else emit Escape. Pinned as a pending spec in test/Hat/Server/OptionEffectSpec.hs; see docs/options-audit.md. | id:fd5889c66e79dca6d9507cb31483df749097e708
state handles program args with spaces | id:fdb964af3c2fc53c77025e4a24ab49d6eea9ef93
AUDIT (done): which options actually drive behavior, not just parse/store. Catalog: docs/options-audit.md; executable sweep: test/Hat/Server/OptionEffectSpec.hs. 33/34 options behavior-verified; found+fixed pane-base-index and escape-time (bug fd). Remaining: display-time left plumbed (timed toast, no sleep-free test). | id:ffa202d4b2e3dd40109c072783bc79d70bd74c7e
activity marker raised in current window should be silenced if/when the OS reports focus that bubbles down to that window. notably, if window is currently active, activity marker never needs to be raised at all | id:ffef87abbe6d0a55d7c863e697aee4a6789067e8
